{"type":"standard","title":"Gubbi Gubbi language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Gubbi Gubbi language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q5515391","titles":{"canonical":"Gubbi_Gubbi_language","normalized":"Gubbi Gubbi language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Gubbi Gubbi language</span></span>"},"pageid":35346577,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6a/Map_of_Traditional_Lands_of_Australian_Aboriginal_peoples_in_SE_Qld.png","width":318,"height":321},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6a/Map_of_Traditional_Lands_of_Australian_Aboriginal_peoples_in_SE_Qld.png","width":318,"height":321},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1343168851","tid":"205d0359-1e3d-11f1-bb1b-b586e30da05e","timestamp":"2026-03-12T17:58:51Z","description":"Australian Aboriginal language","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gubbi_Gubbi_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gubbi_Gubbi_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gubbi_Gubbi_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Gubbi_Gubbi_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gubbi_Gubbi_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Gubbi_Gubbi_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gubbi_Gubbi_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Gubbi_Gubbi_language"}},"extract":"Gubbi Gubbi, also spelt Kabi Kabi, is a language of Queensland in Australia, formerly spoken by the Kabi Kabi people of South-east Queensland. The main dialect, Gubbi Gubbi, is extinct, but there are still 24 people with knowledge of the Butchulla dialect, a language spoken by the Butchulla people of K'gari.","extract_html":"<p><b>Gubbi Gubbi</b>, also spelt <b>Kabi Kabi</b>, is a language of Queensland in Australia, formerly spoken by the Kabi Kabi people of South-east Queensland. The main dialect, Gubbi Gubbi, is extinct, but there are still 24 people with knowledge of the <b>Butchulla</b> dialect, a language spoken by the Butchulla people of K'gari.</p>"}